WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.877
- How I like to do it—like,
I like to get jiggy at the line.

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:04.713
Man, let's ride with it.
Oh, 'scuse me.

00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:06.089
- Stop the hate.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:07.549
Appreciate.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:09.384
- It's been a fun year, man.
- Yes, it has.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:10.635
Very fun.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:11.928
And we gonna win on a bang.

00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:13.138
Don't worry about it.
I'm not worried.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:14.347
I'm not worried.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:18.393
♪♪♪

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:19.853
- What do you know?

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.438
The Patriots are in
the Super Bowl, Simms.

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:23.898
- Oh, real shocker, Lefkoe.
- You know who's not?

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:25.942
- Yeah.
Your Eagles?

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:27.360
- No.
- That shirt?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.945
That's definitely not
in the Super Bowl.

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.989
- I kinda think there's
a little Saints flair to it.

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:32.657
- Oh, is that right?
- Right? Don't I look like I could be

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:34.075
walkin' down the street
with a marching band?

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:35.452
- You're gonna start hatin'
on the Saints right away?

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:37.412
- No, I didn't, I didn't do anything.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:39.289
- You brought them up without—
we were trying to talk about—

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:40.832
- They were one of
the four teams that played.

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.917
- We were talking about the Rams
and the Patriots.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.586
- I wanna say this.
- Yes.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:48.631
- To Saints fans—
- Right.
- What happened to you is a travesty.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.842
I wish that upon no fanbase.

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:52.635
And this is complete sincerity.

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:54.512
That was nonsense,
and I apologize.

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:55.847
- Yeah.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:57.182
- I wanna just
get that out there.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.600
- I get you.
That was a brutal call.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.310
- I will say, though,
that the Super Bowl

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.604
does feel weird
from this aspect.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:08.193
2018 felt like Mahomes-Brees,
Chiefs-Saints the whole year.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:10.111
- Yeah.
- The Rams had their moments.

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:12.155
The Patriots always
have their moments.

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:13.823
- Right.
- But I felt like it

00:01:13.823 --> 00:01:15.867
was all leading
towards Chiefs-Saints.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:17.786
- Yeah.
- And I really wanna say—

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.412
- Because we made it
about two people

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.164
Mahomes and Brees.
That's all it was about.

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:22.749
- Oh, you're upset about this?

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.375
- Well, it's just, like—listen, that's
the matchup I wanted to see.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:25.960
- OK, good.
- I get you there.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.545
But I also picked the Patriots
and Rams

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.297
to win those football games
cuz I said

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:31.674
"Hmm, their teams are greater,
even though we have

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:34.219
this sex appeal matchup at the
quarterback position we like."

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:36.679
- Well, then let's say this,
though, for real.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:38.890
We have loved Rodgers
for a long time.
- Yes.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.226
- You are someone that appreciates
great quarterback play.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.811
- No doubt.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:45.146
- What we witnessed this year
with Patrick Mahomes

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:46.523
cannot be forgotten.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.858
And to everyone out there
that's saying

00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:52.862
"We have all these years,
guaranteed," look at Dan Marino.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:53.947
None of this stuff
is guaranteed.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.448
- Nothing.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.866
- We don't know if Mahomes
is gettin' back here.

00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:58.243
We don't know if Tyreek Hill's
gonna be

00:01:58.243 --> 00:01:59.536
at this speed the rest of his career.
- Right.

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:01.121
- We don't know about
Travis Kelce.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:04.332
What we witnessed:
5,000 yards, 50 touchdowns.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:08.336
I just wanted to give it more love.
- We should.
- Because I fell in love

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:10.421
with my favorite quarterback
in the NFL, Patrick Mahomes.

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:11.631
- I mean, I can't even
believe it.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.299
It's blasphemy. Get outta here.
- Patrick Mahomes.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.635
- Sorry, Aaron, we're gonna get
a new host next year.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.970
Don't worry, buddy.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.555
But—
- Wax poetic about Mahomes.

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:20.056
- I mean, it was a special,
special year.

00:02:20.056 --> 00:02:21.057
- It was special!

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:23.184
- Patrick Mahomes, in this day
and age, for what he did

00:02:23.184 --> 00:02:23.893
- Patrick Mahomes, in this day
and age, for what he did

00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:26.229
I mean, guys like Peyton Manning
and Tom Brady

00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:28.773
you know, 50 touchdown passes,
they didn't do that

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.359
until they were
in the middle of their career.

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:32.819
- They already had a Masters,

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.320
a doctorate
in the quarterback position.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.198
- Exactly right.
This guy throws for 5,000 yards

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:39.868
50 touchdowns, has his first year
as a true starter, right.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:40.952
50 touchdowns, has his first year
as a true starter, right.

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:43.496
And all the teams they faced
every week knew that

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.206
that was the No. 1 thing
they had to stop

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:47.375
and he still delivered week
after week after week.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.835
- He's amazing.
- He is amazing.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:52.338
- I told you guys in like
Week 10 or 11

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.132
the Patriots are gettin'
to the Super Bowl.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.009
You're gonna think it's not
happening, it's happening.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:59.179
This is like if you took
Tim Duncan and LeBron James

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.055
like, their streaks
and, like, put them together

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:02.557
and then you added Popovich

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:05.518
and then, like, then,
like, Roger Federer.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.811
- It's—hey.
It's—

00:03:06.811 --> 00:03:07.979
- And then the Yankees
in the '90s.

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:09.480
Like, it's crazy.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.107
- We will never see anything
like this again

00:03:11.107 --> 00:03:12.483
in the history of the NFL.

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:14.652
Bill Belichick is by far
the greatest coach

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:16.321
in the history of the sport.

00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:18.239
I don't think that's even, like,
a point to argue anymore.

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:20.283
Tom Brady, of course,
what he's doing

00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:22.493
the sustained greatness
is amazing.

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.662
But the big thing I wanna say
to everybody out there

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:27.165
about the New England Patriots
is this.

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:28.499
Stop the hate.

00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:30.335
Appreciate.
OK?

00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:32.003
You're not gonna see
this very often.

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.588
This is a rare thing.

00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:35.256
And as much as we all wanna
hate the Patriots

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:37.759
and I worked for them,
and I know some of these guys

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:39.135
and I have weeks where I go

00:03:39.135 --> 00:03:40.553
"Damn, I'm sick of hearin'
about 'em.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.138
I hope they lose this week."

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:44.557
It's still phenomenal
what they do.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.059
- It's amazing.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:49.520
- This is the era of salary cap,
free agency.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.023
The league is supposed to be
close and competitive.

00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:53.608
I know.

00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:54.651
I'm goin' off because this is
how amazing it is.

00:03:54.651 --> 00:03:56.027
- No, it's real.
It's real.

00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:57.612
- It's supposed to be close
and competitive.

00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:59.072
They made the rules so we
would have different teams

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.573
be at the top every year

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.325
and the only thing
that's been consistent

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:06.454
is the New England Patriots
for the whole 21st century.

00:04:06.454 --> 00:04:09.165
It's been the New England
Patriots, and I just—

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:11.334
I'm amazed by it.
- Yeah.

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:15.630
- It's like two 49er dynasties.
I mean, that's what it is.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.257
I mean, it's amazing.
It's two Steeler dynasties.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.466
- Belichick called me yesterday
to ask for advice.

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:20.009
- He did?
- I told him to relax.

00:04:20.009 --> 00:04:21.302
- What, he wanted to know
what sweater to wear

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:22.929
for next week, what sweatshirt?
- Damn it.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.806
- I gotta cut these sleeves off.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:26.849
- It's Landon Collins. You're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:29.018
- It's Landon Collins. You're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:04:29.018 --> 00:04:30.687
Uh, that's it.

00:04:32.021 --> 00:04:33.690
- In the process of doing
this show

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.650
I think we've made
some special friendships

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.610
with players and former players.
- Definitely, right.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.280
And I think T.O. and Chad Johnson
are at the top of the list.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.948
- I mean, no doubt about it.
- They're our buddies.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.908
- They, like, wanted to hang out
with us when we were in L.A.

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:46.869
- And we were like,
"Chill, chill, we gotta go."
- "We got plenty of time, seriously."

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:48.663
By the way, they're gonna be
in Atlanta

00:04:48.663 --> 00:04:51.291
so email
simmsandlefkoe@gmail.com

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.583
if you're gonna make it there.

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:53.835
They will be there.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.461
But I'm on Twitter.
- Yeah.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.798
- And I see Chad Johnson go,
"I wanna do my own show

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.634
where we got a wide receiver
and I get to work on him."

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.177
- Right.
- This is that show.

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:05.763
We got Chad Johnson and T.O.

00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:09.392
and Mr. Ridley outta Georgia,
who's gonna be maybe

00:05:09.392 --> 00:05:10.727
a first-round pick
in the NFL draft.

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:11.978
- What's Mr. Ridley's first name?

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.187
- Riley.
Nailed it under pressure.

00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:14.772
- And his brother
is Calvin Ridley.

00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:16.566
- Nailed it under pressure.
- You almost choked there.

00:05:16.566 --> 00:05:19.402
But yes, this is your big
audition, T.O. and Ochocinco.

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:21.070
- Yeah.
- Show us what you got.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.530
But seriously, they are gonna
show us what they got.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.490
- They got it.
- Here's two guys that I know

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.701
through my just knowing
people in football.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.244
Yeah, they're ultra-talented.

00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.455
Yeah, it's great touchdown
dances and all that.

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:32.707
But they are obsessed
with their craft.

00:05:32.707 --> 00:05:34.292
They were obsessed
with route-running

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:36.794
and NFL receivers
still go work with them

00:05:36.794 --> 00:05:37.837
to clean up their game.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.088
- And here's why.

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:41.799
- You see I got the shirt
tucked in, right?

00:05:41.799 --> 00:05:43.217
- That don't mean nothing to me.
- You know what that means?

00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:44.427
- No, I don't know what it means.

00:05:44.427 --> 00:05:46.262
- I got this shirt
tucked in, right?
- What's that mean?

00:05:46.262 --> 00:05:47.513
- That means you learned how
to put your shirt in your pants.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.890
- Listen, when you go on a job

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.016
don't you go
with your shirt tucked in?

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.018
Cuz you mean business, right?

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:56.439
Hello.
I am Chad Johnson.

00:05:56.439 --> 00:05:58.441
I am here with my good friend

00:05:58.441 --> 00:06:01.819
and Hall of Fame
receiver Terrell Owens

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:05.573
and up-and-coming
draft prospect

00:06:05.573 --> 00:06:10.495
one of the best receivers
in the nation, Riley Ridley.

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:15.291
- Riley Ridley stepping up!
- Touchdown, Riley Ridley.

00:06:15.291 --> 00:06:18.002
- Touchdown, Georgia!

00:06:18.002 --> 00:06:21.381
- What do you feel like your
best asset is as a receiver?

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.299
- Right now, I'm physical.
- OK.

00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:25.259
- I'm physical, more physical
than any receiver

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:26.344
going into the draft.

00:06:26.344 --> 00:06:28.304
I'm more physical than any DB.

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:30.390
- So that's something that
you don't have to work on.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:34.143
So now, you gotta worry about—
work on the finesse part of the game.

00:06:34.143 --> 00:06:37.355
- So you got T: muscle.
- Right.
- Physical.

00:06:37.355 --> 00:06:39.857
- Physical, get through you,
and then you have my skill set

00:06:39.857 --> 00:06:42.110
where it's completely opposite.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.861
"Don't touch me."

00:06:43.861 --> 00:06:46.614
How I like to do it—like,
I like to get jiggy at the line.

00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:48.032
Man, let's ride with it.

00:06:48.032 --> 00:06:50.118
Oh, 'scuse me.
And I need all this space.

00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:52.161
- My coach said—
he said this to me

00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:54.122
because he knew
I liked basketball.

00:06:54.122 --> 00:06:56.290
- Right.
- And this is what clicked for me.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.127
He said you have to treat
the defensive back

00:06:59.127 --> 00:07:00.878
like you're playin' one-on-one.

00:07:00.878 --> 00:07:02.797
If you playin' one-on-one
and you tryin' to get by me

00:07:02.797 --> 00:07:04.424
what are you gonna do?

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.550
- I'm gonna make some moves.
- You gotta make me move.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.009
- Right.

00:07:07.009 --> 00:07:08.594
- Same thing with every route,
pretty much

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.763
cuz I'm tryin'
to score a bucket.

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.015
- That's what I'm tryin' to get at.
I'm here.

00:07:13.015 --> 00:07:14.308
I'm gonna give you two steps

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:15.518
and then I'm gettin'
right into this.

00:07:15.518 --> 00:07:17.270
- OK, show me.
- So I'm here, and I'm gone.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.855
- OK.

00:07:18.855 --> 00:07:21.107
Initially when you came off
the ball, boom-boom

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.859
you kinda
got wide a little bit.

00:07:22.859 --> 00:07:24.694
Try to stay a little—

00:07:24.694 --> 00:07:26.487
Try to engage them a little bit
more, you know what I mean?
- Absolutely, mhmm.

00:07:26.487 --> 00:07:28.072
- So I like what you did.

00:07:28.072 --> 00:07:30.533
Boom-boom-boom, here,
then kinda get into him.

00:07:30.533 --> 00:07:32.160
Invite him.
Invite him.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.621
And when you here, you wanna
show that acceleration

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.957
like you about to go deep.
- Deep.
- Then you stop.

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:40.501
My problem was, when I used
to get it going in my breaks

00:07:40.501 --> 00:07:44.464
I used to—yeah, I used to have
these flappers right here.

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.048
Then my coach told me

00:07:46.048 --> 00:07:48.134
I had to be a drummer boy,
you know what I mean?

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.385
Be a drummer boy.

00:07:49.385 --> 00:07:51.137
Then when I did, when I did it here

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.639
transition, it's in
and out of my breaks quick.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.057
- Right.

00:07:55.057 --> 00:07:56.267
- We're trying to get you
to become a salesman

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:57.852
before you actually a salesman.

00:07:57.852 --> 00:08:02.690
I do a dig route based off
a, off a comeback stance.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.193
I call it send the dude
to the Gatorade.

00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:06.861
I'm gonna send him
to the Gatorade.

00:08:06.861 --> 00:08:09.363
So, just say—
come here, come in here.

00:08:09.363 --> 00:08:11.199
Just say the ball is in there.

00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:13.284
- Right.
- The ball is in there.

00:08:13.284 --> 00:08:15.203
And I got a dig route.

00:08:15.203 --> 00:08:16.871
So this is what I'm gonna do.

00:08:16.871 --> 00:08:19.624
Boom, boom,
I'm gonna get him right here.

00:08:19.624 --> 00:08:23.419
Aha.
I—oooh.

00:08:23.419 --> 00:08:24.837
I'mma send him
to the Gatorade.

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:27.673
- No doubt.
- All this right here is open.

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:30.760
Cuz as soon as you nod
that way, he gone.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:35.223
- And very seldom on deep balls
do you just blow by a dude.

00:08:35.223 --> 00:08:37.141
That ain't happenin'.
- Yeah.

00:08:37.141 --> 00:08:38.601
- That ain't happenin'

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:39.644
unless you just beat
somebody off the line.

00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:41.312
You just gas him.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:08:41.312 --> 00:08:44.315
- I mean, you got to be
goddamn Tyreek Hill or some—

00:08:44.315 --> 00:08:46.901
That's a different ballgame.
- Randy is one of those guys.

00:08:46.901 --> 00:08:48.361
